The Day 254 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md (about 8.5 KB). It wasn't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused the file and the || true commit did nothing. The file is on disk for the planner.

Top recommendation: #1159, which @yuanhao filed. Its first step, moving to yoagent 0.27.5, already landed (612cd699). Its two code items are still open:
• Item 1: the bash tool drops the end of long output. Past 256 KB, StreamingBashTool (src/tools.rs:537-546) stops adding lines, so everything after that is lost. The outer truncation wrapper keeps a start and an end, but it works on text that was already cut, so its "end" is just the end of the first 256 KB. The model never sees the real last line, such as cargo test's test result:. yoagent 0.27.5's own bash already keeps both ends, so the fix belongs in yoyo's inner accumulator.
• Item 2: checkpoint stops now leave a marker. In checkpoint mode yoyo's turn hook returns false, and on 0.27.5 that adds an [Agent stopped: on_before_turn ended the run] message to the history. No test yet checks what -p, JSON output or the REPL print after that marker.

Second: #1160. By reading only, the guessed-limits note tells Bedrock users replies are "capped at 16000", but Bedrock seems to send a limit only when the user sets one. It's the same shape as last night's Google fix (#1158), and that fix's fake-server test (tests/google_max_tokens_request.rs) can be copied to check it.

Size-gate hazards: these are the tasks most likely to be reverted.
• src/context.rs is 2035 lines and not on the exception list; 16 more lines makes cargo test fail.
• src/config.rs is 90 lines over its recorded size; 11 more lines is fatal.
• src/tools.rs, which #1159 item 1 edits, has no slack left. New logic and tests should go in a separate file, or its recorded size gets updated.

Health: the binary answered a -p prompt correctly. The last 10 sessions finished 2/2 tasks each, with no reverts and no provider errors, and CI is green. I didn't run any targeted tests this time.

Held for owner decisions:
• #1094 item 1 is waiting on @yuanhao's pick, so nothing should ship there.
• #1102 now only records misfires, because he chose to keep refusing (A, answered on #1149).

Research: I compared Claude Code 2.1.319 and Codex 0.167 release notes against yoyo and saved the comparison to yopedia. yopedia's question endpoint said "Sign in required", so I couldn't read the Day 253 scan in full.
• One Claude Code fix makes a broad deny rule win over a narrower allow rule. yoyo already does that, since deny rules are checked first.
• Three ideas are worth a look but untested in yoyo: Claude Code's option to deny instead of waiting on a permission prompt, its /rename fix for reporting success when the save failed, and Codex counting output from failed responses in context accounting.
